# shell: desktop
# PVS-024/PVS-029: a sweep from empty space selects what it crosses.  This
# shell had no band at all -- the only way to gather several icons was one
# modifier click at a time.
key 1 ctrl
wait 10
note a press alone is not a sweep: nothing is drawn until the pointer has
note moved past the slop, so a click that clears the selection does not
note flash a rectangle
press 60 200
move 62 201
wait 2
expect-pixel 61 200 ffffff
release 62 201
wait 2
note a press on empty space and a drag across the first row
press 60 94
move 200 109
move 460 139
release 460 139
wait 5
expect-selected 4
note and a sweep over nothing clears it again
press 60 279
move 200 319
release 200 319
wait 5
expect-selected 0
note the click that starts a sweep also ends a half-finished double click:
note clicking an icon, then the space beside it, then the icon again is
note three separate clicks and must not open anything
click 88 119
wait 2
click 150 119
wait 2
click 88 119
wait 5
expect-windows 1
note and a LIST is swept by the same rectangle: from the empty space
note below the last row, up across the two rows above it
key 3 ctrl
wait 6
press 300 259
move 320 199
move 340 151
wait 3
expect-selected 2
expect-selected-name b.txt
release 340 131
wait 3
expect-selected 2
quit
